{
  "_comment": "Answer-quality cases for ask_mailbox over the synthetic baseline mailbox (indexer/tests/baseline/corpus.py). Synthetic data only: never add a case built from a real mailbox. Message refs 'tNN.M' mean 'tNN.M@baseline.example'; thread refs 'tNN' mean the thread rooted at 'tNN.1@baseline.example'. required_evidence is a list of groups: every group is required and any one ref inside a group satisfies it. Each expected fact lists the message refs and a short verbatim excerpt of the indexed text that establishes it; make baseline checks each excerpt is in that message's indexed text, so references stay independent of what the system retrieves. deterministic.must_include is a list of groups of acceptable spellings (every group required, any spelling in a group satisfies it, case-insensitive substring of the answer); must_not_include lists strings no answer may contain. criteria say which rubric dimensions apply; the judge may not mark an applicable one not_applicable. held_out must equal tests/agent_metrics.py is_held_out(id); never tune against held-out cases. review records that the expected facts were drafted with AI from the synthetic corpus and await owner verification.",
